  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a medical policy denial rather than a data or eligibility error, so resubmission or correction is not appropriate. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is the most effective next step to challenge the bundling determination before escalating to a formal appeal. The patient has no cost-sharing, so billing the patient is not an option, and secondary billing is premature while the primary denial is unresolved.",
